    "id": "obj_1",
    "text": "Add by making the next hundred. Break one number into parts and move a part.",
    "origin": "adapted",
    "source_ref": {
      "src": "src1",
      "page": "n/a",
      "section": "Lesson objective"
    }
  },
  "prerequisite_ids": [],
  "explanations": [
    {
      "id": "exp_1",
      "title": "Tens work like ones",
      "text": "17 plus 13 makes 30. So 17 tens plus 13 tens makes 30 tens. 30 tens is 300.",
      "asset_ids": [],
      "origin": "adapted",
      "source_ref": {
        "src": "src1",
        "page": "n/a",
        "section": "Concept Development"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "exp_2",
      "title": "Number bond to make a hundred",
      "text": "In 190 plus 120, 190 is close to 200. Break 120 into 110 and 10. Now add 200 plus 110.",
      "asset_ids": [
        "a_bond"
      ],
      "origin": "adapted",
      "source_ref": {
        "src": "src1",
        "page": "n/a",
        "section": "Concept Development"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "exp_3",
      "title": "Make a hundred with ones",
      "text": "199 is 1 away from 200. Break 25 into 24 and 1. Now add 200 plus 24.",
      "asset_ids": [
        "a_bond"
      ],
      "origin": "adapted",
      "source_ref": {
        "src": "src1",
        "page": "n/a",
        "section": "Concept Development"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "exp_4",
      "title": "Move from the other number",
      "text": "397 is 3 away from 400. Take 3 from 535 and give it to 397. Now add 532 plus 400.",
      "asset_ids": [
        "a_bond"
      ],
      "origin": "adapted",
      "source_ref": {
        "src": "src1",
        "page": "n/a",
        "section": "Concept Development"
      }
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "ex_1",
      "title": "190 plus 120",
      "text": "Break 120 into 110 and 10. 190 plus 10 is 200. Then 200 plus 110 is 310.",
      "asset_ids": [
        "a_bond"
      ],
      "origin": "adapted",
      "source_ref": {
        "src": "src1",
        "page": "n/a",
        "section": "Concept Development"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ex_2",
      "title": "295 plus 78",
      "text": "Break 78 into 5 and 73. 295 plus 5 is 300. Then 300 plus 73 is 373.",
      "asset_ids": [
        "a_bond"
      ],
      "origin": "adapted",
      "source_ref": {
        "src": "src1",
        "page": "n/a",
        "section": "Concept Development"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ex_3",
      "title": "535 plus 397",
